# DESCRIPTION
# Base-5 subtraction problems to help with the understanding of the standard
# subtraction algorithm.
# ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Other Number Systems')
## DBsection('Base 5 Numbers')
## KEYWORDS('base 5', 'subtraction')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextBaseN.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('BaseN')->setBase(5);

# In this context Real converts a decimal to a base-5 number.
$a1    = Real(random(25, 124));
$b1    = Real(random(5,  24));
$diff1 = $a1 - $b1;

do {
    $a2 = Real(random(25, 124));
    $b2 = Real(random(25, 124));
} until ($a2->value - $b2->value > 5);
$diff2 = $a2 - $b2;

$a3    = Real(random(125, 624));
$b3    = $a3 - Real(random(26, 124));
$diff3 = $a3 - $b3;

# Don't allow students to enter arithmetic operations.
Context('LimitedBaseN')->setBase(5);
$ans1 = Real($diff1->value);
$ans2 = Real($diff2->value);
$ans3 = Real($diff3->value);

BEGIN_PGML

Each of the follow are subtraction problems in base-5.  Find the solution of each without converting to decimal.

1. [`[$a1]_5-[$b1]_5`]=[________]{$ans1}[`_5`]

2. [`[$a2]_5-[$b2]_5`]=[________]{$ans2}[`_5`]

3. [`[$a3]_5-[$b3]_5`]=[________]{$ans3}[`_5`]

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
For each of these problem, you can use a chip/coin model or equivalently the column algorithm, recalling that all of the rebundling (aka borrowing) occurs in base-5. The results are:

1. [`[$a1]_5-[$b1]_5 = [$ans1]_5`]

2. [`[$a2]_5-[$b2]_5 = [$ans2]_5`]

3. [`[$a3]_5-[$b3]_5 = [$ans3]_5`]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
